🍕 The Great Pizza Analytics Challenge – SQL Project
📌 Project Overview

This project is part of the Great Pizza Analytics Challenge, where I acted as a Data Analyst for IDC Pizza and analyzed raw pizza sales data using SQL to generate meaningful business insights.

The goal was to practice real-world data analysis concepts and strengthen SQL skills through hands-on queries.

🛠️ Skills & Concepts Used

Database creation & table design

Data filtering using WHERE, IN, BETWEEN, LIKE, AND / OR / NOT

Aggregations using SUM, AVG, COUNT, MIN, MAX

Grouping using GROUP BY and filtering with HAVING

Joins: INNER JOIN, LEFT JOIN, RIGHT JOIN, FULL OUTER JOIN, SELF JOIN

Data cleaning using DISTINCT, COALESCE, and handling NULL values

📊 Project Tasks

Some key analyses performed in this project:

Identified unique pizza categories

Handled missing values in ingredients

Filtered pizzas by size, price, and name

Calculated total sales and revenue per order

Found top-selling categories

Identified pizzas that were never ordered

Compared price differences across pizza sizes

🚀 What I Learned

Writing efficient SQL queries

Data cleaning and transformation

Business-focused data analysis

Query optimization and performance thinking

